<Layouts.public flash={@flash} current_user={@current_user}>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl space-y-8">
    <.header>
      Privacy policy
      <:subtitle>What we collect, what we never collect, and how your data is handled.</:subtitle>
    </.header>

    <p class="text-xs text-ink-subtle">
      Last updated: November 4, 2026
      <%!-- set at the pre-merge push; the
      final push after sign-off re-verifies the date --%>
    </p>

    <%!-- fv332 D5: the privacy text of record. Plain English, not
        gettext — this template is the policy's wording, same as the
        terms. Every statement below describes what the platform
        actually does today (verified against the code, Nov 4 2026).
        Advisory edits land here. The copy rules apply: plain
        sentences, no em-dashes, no semicolons. --%>
    <.card class="space-y-4" data-testid="privacy-policy">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">About this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        This policy explains how FLUXVALE INFORMATION SOLUTIONS OPC
        ("FluxVale", "we", "us") handles personal data when you use
        FluxVale, our managed cloud platform for open source apps.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        It covers the platform itself. The apps you deploy are
        independent open source projects, and they may have their own
        accounts and their own policies for the data you give them.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        FluxVale is not offered to children. You must be able to form a
        binding contract to hold an account, as the
        <.link navigate={~p"/policies/terms"} class="underline underline-offset-2 hover:text-ink">
          Terms of Service
        </.link>
        say.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">What we collect</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Account data: your email address or addresses, which one is
        primary, the username on your account, and your sign-in
        history.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Billing data: your wallet balance, the record of credit and
        usage entries on it, the order references a payment gives us,
        and the billing country a checkout reports for tax.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Instance data: which apps you deploy, their names and chosen
        sizes, their exposure settings, and their status history.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Operational data: server logs that keep the platform running.
        They include IP addresses, browser details, timestamps, and
        the pages and paths requested.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">What we never collect</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We never see your card details. Payments run through a payment
        provider, and only the provider handles them. What reaches us
        is the payment's outcome and its order reference.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        The site runs no analytics and no advertising trackers. There
        are no tracking cookies and no third-party trackers on our
        pages. The only cookies we set are your signed-in session and
        the standard request token that protects forms.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We do not read, scan, or mine the data inside your apps. Your
        app data belongs to you, and we do not sell, share, or use it
        for our own purposes.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Where your app data lives</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Each instance runs in its own isolated space with its own
        storage. That is where the app's own data lives, such as a
        forge's repositories or a library app's catalog.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Instance backups, when you turn them on, go to storage you
        bring. You supply the bucket and the keys, so those copies stay
        under your control.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We keep our own backups of the platform's control data, which
        covers accounts, billing, and instance settings. Those backups
        do not contain your app data.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Email we send</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Every email we send is transactional, tied to something you
        did: a sign-in code, a payment receipt, a notice about your
        account. There is no marketing mailing list.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Sign-in codes are single use, stored only as cryptographic
        hashes, and they expire ten minutes after we send them.
        Delivery runs through Postmark, our email provider.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Logs and monitoring</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We keep server and application logs to operate the platform
        and to debug problems. Logs hold IP addresses, browser
        details, and request paths for a limited window, and then they
        age out.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Operational metrics and logs are sent to Grafana Cloud, our
        monitoring service, for the same purpose. We do not use them
        to profile you.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">How long we keep data</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Account, billing, and instance data stays while your account
        exists. Sign-in codes are destroyed the moment they are used,
        or when they expire. Logs age out after their limited window.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Financial records are the one category that outlives an
        account. Bookkeeping law in the Philippines requires us to
        keep them for a set period, so those records remain after an
        account is deleted. They carry amounts and references, never
        app data or message content.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Deleting your data</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        You can destroy an instance at any time. Destroying an
        instance deletes it and its data for good. Stopping an
        instance only pauses it, and its storage stays.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        To delete your account, write to admin@fluxvale.com. Deleting
        an account destroys its instances and removes its sign-in
        access. The financial records described above are kept for the
        period the law requires, and we say so plainly instead of
        implying total erasure.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Security</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Traffic to and from the platform is encrypted in transit.
        Sign-in codes, session tokens, and personal access tokens are
        stored as cryptographic hashes, not as readable values.
        Operational secrets live in a hardened vault, not in code or
        configuration files.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Every action on the platform passes an authorization check, so
        one account cannot read or change another account's data.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">Your choices</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        You can add or remove email addresses on your account, rename
        it, sign out of every session at once, and revoke personal
        access tokens yourself from the app.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        To ask what we hold about you, to correct it, or to ask for
        its deletion, write to admin@fluxvale.com. For product help,
        write to support@fluxvale.com.
      </p>
    </.card>

    <.card class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-base font-medium text-ink">The law and changes to this policy</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We handle personal data under the laws of the Philippines,
        including its Data Privacy Act.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        We may change this policy. We give notice before a change
        applies, by email or a note in the app.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-ink-muted">
        Questions about privacy: admin@fluxvale.com
      </p>
    </.card>
  </div>
</Layouts.public>
